# Local development only (see CONTRIBUTING.md). Optional: copy to .dev.vars
# (gitignored) to change the defaults below.
#   cp .dev.vars.example .dev.vars
#
# Deploy to Cloudflare reads this file for the secrets a deployment needs.
# It needs none, so everything here stays commented out.
#
# On localhost you are signed in as dev@localhost, an admin, in the org
# "local". Production builds leave this sign-in bypass out entirely.
# DEV_AUTH_EMAIL=someone@localhost   # sign in as someone else
# DEV_AS_MEMBER=on                   # try powerhouse as a member
#
# Push notifications: run `bun run push:keys` to add VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY,
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY and VAPID_SUBJECT here. Without them, the Notifications
# switch in Settings says push is not set up.
#
# Everything else comes from wrangler.local.jsonc, which local dev merges in
# like a deploy does: with an AI Gateway set up there, local jobs use Claude
# or GPT through it, and with "remote": true bindings, local dev uses (and
# bills) your real browser and email.
